i.MX95 fsl-edma child-node overlay tests
========================================

These overlays exercise the error paths introduced by per-channel DT child
node support in fsl-edma.  They are intended for board testing only and are
not part of the upstream edma series.

Mainline does not provide /sys/kernel/config/device-tree.  The helper module
of-overlay-test.ko applies a .dtbo with of_overlay_fdt_apply() and removes it
on unload.  The .dtbo is loaded through request_firmware_direct().

Requirements
------------

- CONFIG_OF_OVERLAY=y
- CONFIG_FW_LOADER=y
- A kernel build directory to build of-overlay-test.ko
- scripts/dtc/dtc
- No DMA client using the controller

The overlays target edma2 channel 63 (dma-channel@42208000).  Channels 0 and 1
are already marked unavailable by the base DTS.

The script verifies that the running DT contains
/sys/firmware/devicetree/base/soc/bus@42000000/dma-controller@42000000/dma-channel@42208000
and refuses to run if the booted DTB was not built from the converted
imx95.dtsi.  With dma-channel-mask = <0x3>, dma0chan0 and dma0chan1 must not
be registered; if they are present, the running DTB does not match this
series.

Running
-------

  sudo ./test-edma-overlays.sh

The script:

1. compiles the .dtso files with dtc;
2. installs the .dtbo files under /lib/firmware/edma-test;
3. builds of-overlay-test.ko if needed;
4. unbinds fsl-edma;
5. loads the module to apply one overlay;
6. rebinds fsl-edma and checks the result;
7. unloads the module to remove the overlay and restores the base tree.

Environment overrides:

  DRV=fsl-edma
  DEV=42000000.dma-controller
  DTC=/path/to/scripts/dtc/dtc
  KDIR=/lib/modules/$(uname -r)/build
  MODULE=/path/to/of-overlay-test.ko
  FW_DIR=/lib/firmware/edma-test

Test matrix
-----------

  imx95-edma-chan63-disabled.dtso
      Disable the channel 63 child node without masking it.
      Expected: probe fails with
      "has no dma-channel child node".

  imx95-edma-chan63-disabled-masked.dtso
      Disable the child node and set bit 63 in dma-channel-mask.
      Expected: probe succeeds and channel 63 is absent.

  imx95-edma-chan63-masked.dtso
      Keep the child node but set bit 63 in dma-channel-mask.
      Expected: probe succeeds and channel 63 is absent.

  imx95-edma-chan63-no-irq.dtso
      Break the interrupts specifier of the channel 63 child node.  A base
      property cannot be deleted by an overlay, so it is replaced with a
      truncated specifier.
      Expected: probe fails with
      "child node has no valid interrupt".

  imx95-edma-chan63-unaligned.dtso
      Move the channel 63 reg to an unaligned address.
      Expected: probe fails with "invalid channel".

  imx95-edma-chan63-outside.dtso
      Move the channel 63 reg outside the controller range.
      Expected: probe fails with "invalid channel".

  imx95-edma-dma-channels-63.dtso
      Reduce dma-channels to 63 while leaving all 64 child nodes.
      Expected: probe succeeds and channel 63 is ignored.

Note: the overlay target paths assume the i.MX95 node hierarchy
/soc/bus@42000000/dma-controller@42000000.  Adjust them if the board uses a
different base tree.
